course: dictionary
lesson: 13605
title: Incubate: keeping things warm to grow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Incubate is one of them. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning fits. «The hen sat on her eggs to incubate them.» The eggs need warmth, and a hen sitting on them gives that warmth, so incubate means to keep eggs warm until they hatch.
explain: The same word can be used for germs or babies. «The germs incubated in his body for two days before he felt ill.» Here the germs were growing inside him before he had any sign of sickness. Ask yourself: what is being kept warm, and what is it waiting to do? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Incubate is a verb, so its forms change: incubate, incubates, incubated, incubating. «Our class will incubate duck eggs next term.» Look for the clue words, like eggs, germs or babies, and they will show you which meaning you need.
fact: Incubate means to keep eggs warm so they will hatch.
fact: A hen incubates her eggs by sitting on them, and a machine can do the same job.
fact: Incubate can also mean to keep something, like germs or a tiny premature baby, at the right warm temperature.
fact: In medicine, an illness that incubates is growing in the body before you feel sick. The time between catching a germ and feeling ill is called the incubation period.
fact: Incubate can also mean to develop an idea slowly before it is ready. Context tells you which meaning is right.
exercise: «The hen sat on her eggs to incubate them.» What does incubate mean here? | To break the eggs open | *To keep the eggs warm so they hatch | To paint the eggs | To count the eggs
exercise: «The germs incubated in his body for two days before he felt ill.» What does incubated mean? | To wash the germs away | To be sent home from school | *To grow inside the body before any sickness shows | To spread out and be cured quickly
exercise: In health lessons, what is an incubation period? | The time a cold lasts after you feel better | The time a hen takes to lay an egg | *The time between catching a germ and feeling ill | The time a baby sleeps in an incubator
test: Which word is closest in meaning to incubate when it means keeping eggs warm? | Freeze | Sell | *Keep warm | Hide
test: Which word means to keep something warm so it can grow? | Freeze | Chill | *Incubate | Cool
exam: «The inventor spent three years incubating her idea before the company opened.» What does incubating mean here? | Throwing the idea away | Telling everyone about it straight away | *Developing the idea slowly before it is ready | Selling the idea at once
